1 OPEN

   Opens a file for READ and WRITE, and gives it a logical name.

   Format

     OPEN logical-name[:] filespec

2 Parameters

 logical-name[:]

   The name READ, WRITE, and CLOSE know the file by, defined in the
   process table at supervisor mode.  A logical name OPEN already has a
   file for gets no other: OPEN then does nothing.

 filespec

   The file, on a mounted volume or on the host, by the usual rules.
   Its type is .DAT unless one is given.

2 Description

   The file stays open until CLOSE closes it, even after the command
   procedure that opened it ends.  A file OPEN makes has variable-length
   records with two bytes of fixed control (VFC), and print-file
   carriage control.

   A file that can't be opened is reported as

     %DCL-E-OPENIN, error opening DUA0:[WORK]NOSUCH.DAT; as input
     -RMS-E-FNF, file not found

   (OPENOUT for a new file), and $STATUS is RMS's status.  The logical
   name is the way to the file: TYPE of it types the file from where
   READ has got to, and once it is deassigned, READ and CLOSE can't
   reach the file.

2 Qualifiers
/APPEND

   Opens an existing file to write at its end.  It can't be given with
   /WRITE.

/ERROR

      /ERROR=label

   In a command procedure, goes to the label if the file can't be
   opened, with no message and no ON action.

/HOST

   After the filespec, makes it a host file name, whatever it looks
   like.

/READ

   Opens an existing file to read (the default).  With /WRITE, opens an
   existing file to read and write, at its start.

/SHARE

      /SHARE[=keyword]

   Lets other users of the file read it (READ), or read and write it
   (WRITE, the default keyword).  Without /SHARE, others may read a file
   opened to read, and nothing may open a file opened to write, not
   even TYPE.

/WRITE

   Makes a new file, the next version, to write.  With /READ, opens an
   existing one to read and write.

2 Examples

   1.$ OPEN/WRITE OUT RESULTS.DAT
     $ WRITE OUT "Count is ", COUNT
     $ CLOSE OUT

     Writes one record to a new RESULTS.DAT.

   2.$ OPEN/READ/WRITE/SHARE=WRITE PARTS PARTS.IDX

     Opens an indexed file to read and change, sharing it with other
     processes.
